WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.142
A lead comes in.

00:00:02.142 --> 00:00:05.746
Then a deal, a meeting, a follow-up, and an invoice.

00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:09.350
In DryKraft, each step carries the customer context forward.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.620
Start with your own workspace.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.845
Choose its address, time zone, and the currencies your team uses.

00:00:18.845 --> 00:00:23.070
The same navigation follows you from your desk to your phone.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:35.520
Bring in a CSV and preview the mapping before you apply it.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.332
Keep people, companies, leads, and tasks together.

00:00:38.332 --> 00:00:45.160
Save smart lists and use related records, notes, activity, and owners to see who does what next.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.450
A new lead can create a linked deal in Sales.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.950
Move the opportunity through your own stages, review its history, and see what the pipeline is worth in each currency.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.033
Find the appointment in month view or the agenda.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:15.366
Set availability, assign hosts, and share a booking link.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:19.440
Connect a Google or Outlook calendar when your team needs it.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.651
Write a campaign or a timed sequence.

00:01:30.651 --> 00:01:35.288
Preview the message and review exactly who is eligible before launch.

00:01:35.288 --> 00:01:44.140
Connect email, SMS, AI voice, or WhatsApp, then see what the provider accepted and whether a reply stopped the next step.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.766
With email warmup, set a starting daily allowance, an increase, and a target.

00:02:00.766 --> 00:02:04.274
Campaigns, sequences, and workflow emails share that mailbox allowance.

00:02:04.274 --> 00:02:05.833
Extra work stays queued.

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:09.730
Pause, resume, or restart the ramp from the same panel.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:19.422
Start an invoice from the linked deal, apply a template, and issue the PDF.

00:02:19.422 --> 00:02:21.466
Record payments you received elsewhere.

00:02:21.466 --> 00:02:26.780
Create purchase orders, submit expenses for approval, and keep totals meaningful across currencies.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:44.212
Publish a workflow that creates a task when a customer record changes.

00:02:44.212 --> 00:02:49.100
DryKraft saves the change and its event together in the transactional outbox.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:54.740
A worker processes eligible events, and the resulting workflow or webhook has its own history.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.639
Add custom objects and relationships.

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:15.843
Choose the columns you need, build a dashboard with your own measures, and export a report.

00:03:15.843 --> 00:03:19.720
Save templates your team can reuse across finance and outreach.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:28.718
Invite teammates, assign roles, and organize teams and locations.

00:03:28.718 --> 00:03:33.182
Secure accounts with two-step verification, recovery codes, and session controls.

00:03:33.182 --> 00:03:37.200
Give integrations scoped API keys and inspect webhook deliveries.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.363
Separate platform and reseller consoles manage customers and access.

00:03:47.363 --> 00:03:51.839
Platform staff can provision workspaces, invite owners, and review delivery history.

00:03:51.839 --> 00:03:57.130
Resellers can manage their organization, staff, retail plans, and customer workspaces where enabled.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:11.982
From the first conversation to the next action, keep the whole customer journey connected.

00:04:11.982 --> 00:04:15.000
Explore DryKraft at drykraft.com.
